course: dictionary
lesson: 12964
title: One word, many jobs: executing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some verbs change their ending to show that something is happening right now. «Executing» comes from the verb «execute», which means to carry out or to do. The «-ing» ending tells you the action is going on.
explain: «The team is executing a clever plan to win the match.» Look at the clues: a plan and a match. A team with a plan is trying to do something. So executing means carrying out the plan. Check it by swapping in «carrying out» and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In computing, a computer is executing a program when it runs the instructions one step at a time. «The computer is executing the code, line by line.» The clues are computer and code, so here executing means running the steps.
explain: The same word can have different meanings in different subjects. Look at the topic around it. Plan, order, move, and code are all clues that the meaning is about doing something.
fact: «Executing» is the «-ing» form of the verb «execute».
fact: «Executing» can mean carrying out a plan, an order, a task, or a movement.
fact: «Executing» can also mean running a program or instruction on a computer.
fact: In history, «executing» has a much older, harsher meaning: putting someone to death by law. You will meet this meaning in history books, but it is not used in everyday lessons.
fact: When you are unsure which meaning is right, swap in «carrying out» or «running» and check if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The class is executing the dance routine together.» What does executing mean here? | Sleeping through | *Carrying out or doing | Forgetting | Shouting loudly
exercise: «The computer is executing the program step by step.» What is the computer doing? | Making a noisy sound | Eating its power | Turning off its screen | *Running the instructions
exercise: Which word means carrying out or doing? | singing | sleeping | *executing | hiding
test: «Mum is executing her plan to surprise Dad.» What does executing mean? | Telling a joke about the plan | Dropping the plan | *Carrying out the plan | Writing a letter about the plan
test: A computer is executing code when it... | *Runs each step in the code | Stops playing its games | Makes a cup of tea | Sings a song to the screen
exam: «Grandad was executing the recipe carefully.» What does executing mean? | Reading only the title | Burning it | *Following and carrying it out | Ignoring it
